{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DistributedTargetInvocationDecoder","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"SerializationRequirement","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Distributed0A23TargetInvocationDecoderP24SerializationRequirementQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedTargetInvocationDecoder\/SerializationRequirement"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Decoding DistributedActor arguments using Codable","anchor":"Decoding-DistributedActor-arguments-using-Codable"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When using an actor system where "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ActorID"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":", every distributed actor using that system"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also implicitly "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" (see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedActorSystem"},{"type":"text","text":"). Such distributed actors are encoded"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as their "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ActorID"},{"type":"text","text":" stored in an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encoder\/singleValueContainer"},{"type":"text","text":". When "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" is being used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by such a system, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"decodeNextArgument"},{"type":"text","text":" method will be using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Decoder"},{"type":"text","text":" to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"decode the incoming values, which may themselves be distributed actors."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An actor system must be provided to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Decoder"},{"type":"text","text":" in order for a distributed actor’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Decodable\/init(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to be able to return the instance of the actor. Specifically, the decoded"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ActorID"},{"type":"text","text":" is passed to the actor system’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"resolve(id:as:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method in order to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"return either a local instance identified by this ID, or creating a remote actor reference."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus, you must set the actor system the decoding is performed for, on the decoder’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userInfo"},{"type":"text","text":", as follows:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["mutating func decodeNextArgument<Argument: SerializationRequirement>() throws -> Argument {","  let argumentData: Data = \/\/\/ ...","  \/\/ ...","  decoder.userInfo[.actorSystemKey] = self.actorSystem","  return try Argument.decode(","}"]}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformingTypes","title":"Conforming Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/LocalTestingInvocationDecoder"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedTargetInvocationDecoder","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"title":"DistributedTargetInvocationDecoder","externalID":"s:11Distributed0A23TargetInvocationDecoderP","symbolKind":"protocol","platforms":[{"beta":false,"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","unavailable":false},{"name":"iPadOS","unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","deprecated":false,"